  "summary": "Two independent read-only R3 reviews find that v42 closes several local identity issues but violates the approved architecture-v28 boundary by expanding a trusted single-process archival verifier into a multi-process FD, sandbox and capacity control plane. The resulting schemas are also internally non-composable for generated output admission, policy ref types, supervisor crash recovery, runtime evidence binding and pipe completion. The required redirect is a mainline-preserving simplification back to one trusted command, read-only frozen inputs and one previously absent output directory.",
